----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE IMPLEMENTATION (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative.*)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Four-file split mirroring the shipped AnnouncerRegion / AiUsageCard surfaces:
  .Model.cs      - Registration (slug, feature id "cabin-temperature-impact-narrative", root automation
                   id ai-feature-cabin-temperature-impact-narrative-root, narrate path, every i18n
                   key+English fallback); AiNarrationStreamState enum (idle/streaming/paused-confirm/
                   done/error - the web AiStreamState union); AiNarrationStreamEvent + AiNarrationSseParser
                   (native port of useAiStream parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent, malformed/unknown -> null,
                   bit-for-bit); AiNarrationRequest ({vehicle_id}); PII-safe diagnostics (view.opened only).
  .Source.cs     - IAiNarrationStreamTransport (P1/S8 seam = the native useAiStream) + production
                   HttpAiNarrationStreamTransport (POST text/event-stream over HttpClient + ITokenProvider,
                   line-reassembled SSE frames; network faults -> classified terminal Error event, never an
                   exception across the enumerator; cancellation propagates). IAiFeatureGate (native
                   useAiEnabled) + StaticAiFeatureGate / DelegateAiFeatureGate.
  .ViewModel.cs  - INotifyPropertyChanged+IDisposable state machine: withAiFeature gate (IsGateOpen),
                   haveInputs guard (CanStart = vehicle_id>0), useAiStream lifecycle (idle->streaming->
                   done/error; duplicate Start no-op; cancel->idle; close-without-terminal->done),
                   offline classification, all localized labels + the "Ask Helix . Narrate impact"
                   accessible name. Validates the feature id against the canonical AiFeatureRegistry
                   (native withAiFeature unknown-id guard).
  .cs            - WinUI 3 ContentControl: tokenized glass card (DisplayTokens), header (PanelTitle title +
                   "Helix" TsBadge + secondary description), TsButton (Outline/Small, IsLoading ring while
                   streaming), streamed-output panel (TsSpinner thinking indicator -> accumulating
                   narration -> danger error row), dispatcher-coalesced render, gate collapses the whole
                   surface when off (no root automation id - matches the web HOC rendering null), Narrator
                   name + Group automation peer, emits view.opened on Loaded.

States reproduced from the web source (every state renders; none hidden):
  gated-off (collapsed, no DOM/automation id) | idle not-ready (vehicle unresolved -> disabled action) |
  idle ready | streaming-thinking (spinner) | streaming-with-text | done (final narration) |
  error (Helix error: <msg>) | offline (connectivity fault -> offline message + retry via the button).
  NOTE: the web source is an on-demand SSE narration card, NOT a cached read; it has no data-freshness
  "stale" branch, so none is fabricated (faithful parity). The connectivity-aware "offline" branch is
  derived honestly from a classified network failure on the stream.

i18n: every string flows through ILocalizer.GetString(key, fallback) with the translation.* catalog
  prefix; keys: tempImpact.aiNarrative.{title,description,generateButton,badge}, helix.{askHelix,thinking,
  errorLabel}, ai.common.errorUnknown, common.offline. English fallbacks verbatim from the web second args.
A11y: card Narrator name = title; action accessible name = "Ask Helix . Narrate impact" (web aria-label);
  output panel is a live region; thinking spinner + error surface announce. No English literals in code.
Telemetry: view.opened slug=AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative on Loaded (P1/S11), PII-safe (never the
  narration text, vehicle id, or prompt input).
Tests (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrativeTests.cs, 40):
  adapter unit tests (SSE parser delta/done/error/tool/confirm + malformed/unknown -> null), per-state
  view-model tests (gate on/off, canStart matrix, streaming->done, no-terminal->done, duplicate-start
  no-op, error, offline, confirm-pause, cancel->idle, retry), and a11y-label tests (action automation
  name, thinking label flip, fallback copy). All via a headless fake transport + PassthroughLocalizer.

