PRE-EXISTING REPO FIXES required to reach a loadable/buildable gate (NOT part of the surface, but
mandatory to run build/test - documented per honesty covenant rule 7 "no predecessor bypass"):
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was CORRUPTED into 3 concatenated <Project>
   roots by the file's documented `.gitattributes merge=union` strategy -> MSB4025 "multiple root
   elements" -> the WHOLE test project (and thus `dotnet test`) could not load at HEAD. Regenerated, per
   the file's own INVARIANT, into exactly ONE <Project> = header + a single ordinal-sorted, deduplicated
   Compile-link ItemGroup of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs under dashboard-widgets/feature-views/
   misc-surfaces/modals-dialogs/shared-surfaces (905 entries = the prior 902 union + this surface's 3
   logic files; proven equal to the prior unique set before adding mine).
2. The regenerated (now-loadable) test project surfaced a latent type collision the corruption had masked:
   a later modals-dialogs surface (WidgetCatalogueDialog) added a SECOND public `WidgetCategory` enum in
   the ModalsDialogs namespace, which shadowed the imported FeatureViews.WidgetCategory inside
   WidgetSettingsModal.Model.cs (same-namespace type beats a using-alias), flipping
   WidgetSettingsProjection.IsVehicleWidget/IsChartWidget to the wrong enum and breaking the
   WidgetCatalogEntry-typed call sites in BOTH TeslaSync.App.csproj (app) AND the test project (CS1503).
   Fixed minimally + correctly with a uniquely-named alias (WidgetCatalogCategory =
   TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.WidgetCategory) in WidgetSettingsModal.Model.cs and a matching
   `using WidgetCategory = ...FeatureViews.WidgetCategory;` disambiguation in WidgetSettingsModalTests.cs.
   No production behaviour changed; restores the pre-collision intent.

